## 6. CL2.2 hypotheses

CL2.2 tests four competing explanations.

```text
H1_DATA_DEPENDENCE:
A generic non-oracle learner improves specifically as lawful safe-ledger training data increases and fails without data or with corrupted targets.
```

```text
H2_PRIOR_DEPENDENCE:
Performance remains high even when training data is removed, reduced, corrupted, or made inconsistent, implying the learner imports too much prior structure.
```

```text
H3_NO_GENERIC_SIGNAL:
When the rule-family prior is removed, generic learners cannot learn transition structure from the safe ledger under the required holdouts.
```

```text
H4_CONTROL_ARTIFACT_PERSISTS:
Negative controls still score too high, so the instrument cannot distinguish data-dependent learning from artifact.
```

The task must decide which hypothesis is best supported.

