## 8. Required learner restrictions

CL2.2 must separate two categories.

---

### 8.1 Evidence-eligible generic learner

This is the only learner allowed to support `DATA-DEPENDENT-LEARNING-OK`.

It must not encode the exact CL1 domain transition family.

Allowed:

```text
- generic tables over learned feature interactions;
- generic decision-tree-like splits over visible input features;
- generic nearest-neighbor / local interpolation over visible input features;
- generic coordinate-wise classifiers or regressors trained from rows;
- standard-library Python only.
```

Forbidden:

```text
- hardcoding AID_i increases zone i;
- hardcoding phase-indexed shock;
- hardcoding failed-zone mass drain;
- hardcoding CONSERVE restores mass;
- hardcoding max zone / max mass update rules from domain.py;
- copying the CL2 RuleFamilyTransitionLearner as evidence;
- calling transition or any oracle function at prediction time.
```

The learner may be simple. It does not need to succeed. Failure is valid evidence.

---

### 8.2 Prior diagnostic learner

The CL2 `RuleFamilyTransitionLearner` may be run only as a diagnostic baseline.

It must be labeled:

```text
PRIOR-DIAGNOSTIC-ONLY
```

It must not be used to support a positive CL2.2 verdict.

Purpose:

> quantify how much performance can be obtained from a transition-family prior.

