## 11. Required diagnostics

---

### 11.1 Zero-fit diagnostic

Train the evidence-eligible generic learner with no target rows or with features only and no target mapping.

Evaluate on structural holdout.

Purpose:

> if zero-fit already performs well, the learner prior is too strong or the evaluation is broken.

Pass condition:

```text
zero_fit_structural_accuracy <= 0.35
```

If it exceeds this threshold, verdict must be:

```text
PRIOR-DEPENDENCE-FAIL
```

or

```text
CONTROL-ARTIFACT-PERSISTS
```

depending on the cause.

---

### 11.2 Learning curve diagnostic

Train the same generic learner on:

```text
1%
5%
20%
100%
```

of the training data.

Use the same source-state and structural holdout tests.

Required metrics:

```text
source_holdout exact accuracy at each data fraction
structural_holdout exact accuracy at each data fraction
coordinate accuracy at each data fraction
```

Pass requires:

```text
full_data_structural_holdout_accuracy - 1_percent_structural_holdout_accuracy >= 0.20
```

and:

```text
full_data_structural_holdout_accuracy - zero_fit_structural_accuracy >= 0.30
```

This is the core data-dependence condition.

---

### 11.3 Corrupted-target controls

Run the evidence-eligible generic learner on these corrupted training sets:

```text
independent_impossible_target
cross_phase_target_shuffle
feature_permutation_control
```

Evaluate on original true holdout targets.

Pass requires:

```text
best_corrupted_target_accuracy <= 0.35
```

and:

```text
full_data_structural_holdout_accuracy - best_corrupted_target_accuracy >= 0.30
```

If corrupted controls remain high, verdict must be:

```text
CONTROL-ARTIFACT-PERSISTS
```

---

### 11.4 Prior diagnostic baseline

Run the CL2 `RuleFamilyTransitionLearner` on the same diagnostics, but label it:

```text
PRIOR-DIAGNOSTIC-ONLY
```

This result cannot support a positive verdict.

If this learner succeeds while the generic learner fails, that supports:

```text
NO-GENERIC-LEARNER-SIGNAL
```

or:

```text
PRIOR-DEPENDENCE-FAIL
```

depending on the generic learner’s zero-fit and corrupted-control behavior.

---

### 11.5 Leakage audit

Check:

```text
- no forbidden fields in rows;
- no forbidden oracle functions called by evidence-eligible learner at prediction time;
- no target fields included in features;
- test targets not used in fit;
- corrupted controls evaluated against original true test targets;
- no source-file lineage or admission labels used as features.
```

Any violation sets verdict to:

```text
CONTROL-ARTIFACT-PERSISTS
```

or:

```text
PRIOR-DEPENDENCE-FAIL
```

if caused by learner prior.

