## 13. Decision rule

Use exactly this decision rule.

```text
DATA-DEPENDENT-LEARNING-OK
iff
no leakage is detected
AND zero_fit_structural_accuracy <= 0.35
AND full_data_source_holdout_accuracy >= 0.70
AND full_data_structural_holdout_accuracy >= 0.65
AND full_data_cross_phase_accuracy >= 0.65
AND data_gain >= 0.30
AND tiny_to_full_gain >= 0.20
AND best_corrupted_target_accuracy <= 0.35
AND corruption_drop >= 0.30
```

```text
PRIOR-DEPENDENCE-FAIL
iff
zero_fit_structural_accuracy > 0.35
OR performance remains high when training labels are removed
OR the evidence-eligible learner encodes the exact transition family
OR the only successful learner is PRIOR-DIAGNOSTIC-ONLY
```

```text
NO-GENERIC-LEARNER-SIGNAL
iff
no leakage is detected
AND zero_fit_structural_accuracy <= 0.35
AND corrupted controls are below threshold
AND generic full-data learner fails any required positive accuracy threshold
```

```text
CONTROL-ARTIFACT-PERSISTS
iff
no direct leakage is detected
AND (
  best_corrupted_target_accuracy > 0.35
  OR feature_permutation_control max_exact > 0.35
  OR corrupted controls disagree in a way that makes the instrument unreliable
)
```

```text
INCONCLUSIVE-DATA-DEPENDENCE
iff
required splits are too small
OR learner implementation cannot run without violating constraints
OR metrics are incomplete
OR no verdict above cleanly applies
```

```text
HALT-GOAL-DRIFT
iff
the work becomes about learner architecture tuning, ML benchmarking, toy-domain exploration, methodology, DSL/CEGIS/meta-synthesis, or substrate-generation theory rather than testing data-dependence of learner performance as a precondition for safe-ledger substrate work
```

If multiple verdicts apply, choose the strongest halt in this order:

```text
HALT-GOAL-DRIFT
CONTROL-ARTIFACT-PERSISTS
PRIOR-DEPENDENCE-FAIL
INCONCLUSIVE-DATA-DEPENDENCE
NO-GENERIC-LEARNER-SIGNAL
DATA-DEPENDENT-LEARNING-OK
```

Important:

`DATA-DEPENDENT-LEARNING-OK` does not mean substrate discovery.

It only means:

> this safe ledger supports a learner whose transition-prediction performance depends on data rather than on an inadmissible prior, under this toy domain and these holdouts.

