* no claim that the learner is safe under arbitrary future actions;
* no claim that the action ledger transfers to other domains;
* no claim that the boundary is learned;
* no claim that the oracle-filtered ledger is available in real domains;
* no claim that data-dependence proves derivability;
* no claim that a general substrate generator exists;
* no claim that the playbook is constructive in general.

---

## 16. Halt-downstream rule

If decision is not `DATA-DEPENDENT-LEARNING-OK`, stop.

Do not run representation analysis.

Do not run autonomous rollout.

Do not train an LLM.

Do not make derivability or substrate claims.

If decision is `DATA-DEPENDENT-LEARNING-OK`, the only allowed next step is a separately pre-registered representation / internal-structure probe.

That next probe must still not claim derivability until tested.

---

## 17. Pass/fail bar for Codex task

The Codex task itself succeeds if it produces a complete CL2.2 report and a valid decision, even if the decision is negative.

The task fails if:

* no pre-registration JSON is written before metrics;
* thresholds are changed after seeing results;
* CL2 RuleFamilyTransitionLearner is used as positive evidence;
* evidence-eligible learner encodes the exact transition family;
* no zero-fit diagnostic is run;
* no learning curve is run;
* no corrupted-target control is run;
* no prior diagnostic baseline is run;
* no prior audit is written;
* no leakage audit is written;
* no durable constraint is written;
* `what was NOT shown` is omitted;
* report claims substrate discovery, derived world-model content, autonomous safety, or LLM safety;
* work turns into learner architecture search, ML benchmarking, DSL/CEGIS/meta-synthesis, or substrate-generation theory.

---

## 18. Final instruction

The desired result is not “learner success.”

The desired result is an honest data-dependence verdict:

> either transition prediction improves because the learner uses safe-ledger data,
> or the apparent learning remains prior-driven, control-confounded, too weak, or inconclusive.

Optimize for survival under criticism, not for recovering the CL2 positive-looking learner scores.

